    {"chapter":"dgram","parent":"UDP/datagram sockets","signatures":["`dgram.createSocket(options[, callback])`","`socket.bind(options[, callback])`"],"status":"partial","reason":"The options forms of createSocket and bind compile and match Node, including a custom lookup: it runs for bind, connect and the unconnected sends — and for the implicit bind a connect or send on an unbound socket resolves first, as Node's bind does — with the operation continuing from its answer. A lookup failure is re-raised as an equivalent Error built from its message, so the program's own error object is not passed through. A failed implicit bind answers on the socket's 'error' event, and a settled socket drops the program's resolver. bind(options) adopts an existing datagram descriptor when options.fd is a positive int32 (any other fd falls through to the port bind, and bindSync ignores fd); the block lists are enforced on the send and receive paths, and createSocket's signal closes the socket on abort.","evidence":["tests/corpus/dgram-socket-class.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-bind-options.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-block-list-receive.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-block-list-send.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-block-list-edges.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-block-list-bind.ts","tests/corpus/compat-dgram-socket.mjs","tests/corpus/compat-dgram-socket.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-signal.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-bind-fd.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-signal-close-removes-listener.cjs","tests/corpus/dgram-custom-lookup.ts","tests/corpus/dgram-lookup-lifecycle.cjs", "tests/corpus/dgram-implicit-bind-failure.ts", "tests/corpus/dgram-lookup-capture.ts"]},
